00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:36.630
<b>Tigre!</b>

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:42.020
<b>Lady Eleonora, where's Sir Tigrevurmud?</b>

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.600
<b>He didn't even make it to his bed.</b>

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.060
<b>I hope he didn't catch a cold.</b>

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:52.110
<b>I wish we could let him sleep a little longer,</b>

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.190
<b>but right now that's out of the question.</b>

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.190
<b>True.</b>

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.990
<b>Now then, how shall we wake him up?</b>

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.950
<b>Normal methods won't work here.</b>

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.200
<b>Lim once did it by thrusting a sword into his mouth.{phallic metaphor?}{Let's keep it to what she actually did.}</b>

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.830
<b>When I tried to copy her, Titta got mad at me.</b>

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.810
<b>I told you, no!</b>

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:12.830
<b>He won't be able to eat breakfast if you do that!{hmm... I don't really get the logic here}{When Elen tried, Titta complained about how shoving a sword down his throat will harm his mouth. In other words, he'll miss out on breakfast since he's all bloody.}</b>

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.760
<b>Wow, he's fast asleep.</b>

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.970
<b>I have an idea.</b>

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:20.590
<b>Oh?</b>

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.220
<b>Tigre said that no matter how exhausted</b>

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:27.350
<b>he was the night before, he'd wake up instantly if he were to sense an animal about to attack.</b>

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:28.390
<b>My...</b>

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:32.730
<b>That's only when he's out hunting, not now.</b>

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.940
<b>What are you planning to do?</b>

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.640
<b>Good morning, Tigre.{Morning grope: check.}</b>

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.020
<b>You woke me with your bloodlust?</b>

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:12.520
<b>Sorry. I won't ever try a stunt like that again.</b>

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.520
<b>I'd appreciate that.{doesn't matter, he'll find a way to get his morning grope in either way.}</b>

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.820
<b>This is quite a feast, huh?</b>

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.150
<b>It's not bad.</b>

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:24.320
<b>The nearby towns and villages sent us all sorts of things.</b>

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.820
<b>They're offering stuff voluntarily, before it can be taken away,</b>

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.870
<b>to get in our good books, aren't they?</b>

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:30.830
<b>So you simply accepted their gifts?</b>

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:33.660
<b>Don't be silly. 
We bought everything.</b>

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:37.170
<b>Then again, it sounds like
we didn't pay all that much.</b>

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:41.170
<b>Ryurik and Gerald are in charge of procurement.</b>

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.300
<b>That explains it.</b>

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.840
<b>Anyway, what's the plan?</b>

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.600
<b>We've got the opportunity
to completely crush Thenardier...</b>

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.060
<b>We head to Artesium.</b>

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.060
<b>We're going to help its inhabitants?</b>

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:57.020
<b>I don't think we have enough supplies for all the citizens.</b>

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.230
<b>No, we're not entering the city itself.</b>

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.070
<b>What do you mean?</b>

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:05.950
<b>We head to its underground from outside
the walls and validate Princess Regin's lineage.</b>

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:07.530
<b>I see.</b>

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:10.790
<b>If we can prove that Princess Regin is indeed royalty,</b>

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.330
<b>our cause will be seen as the <i>only</i> just one.</b>

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:16.960
<b>And then <i>we</i> can condemn <i>Thenardier's</i> actions.</b>

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.380
<b>Your Highness,</b>

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.340
<b>please tell us once again what we should expect under the city of Artesium.</b>

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:28.720
<b>All I know is what my father told me.
I never entered myself.</b>

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.600
<b>Our goal is "Charles' Saint-Groel", the Holy Grotto.</b>

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:35.850
<b>It's said that Charles, the founder of our country,{charlululululululu}</b>

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:39.060
<b>decided to become king after
receiving divine guidance there.</b>

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.650
<b>In other words, it's Brune's birthplace.</b>

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:46.860
<b>As far as I know, there are three entrances to the Holy Grotto:</b>

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.240
<b>One is in the central district of Artesium.</b>

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:56.540
<b>Another is in the Temple of Mossia, 
Mother Goddess of the Land, to the southeast.</b>

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:00.380
<b>The last is in the public cemetery, to the northeast.</b>

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:05.130
<b>The one closest to us is in the Temple of Mossia.</b>

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:07.620
<b>Her Highness and I will head there.</b>

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.550
<b>{Yeah, }Please get it done.</b>

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:19.050
<b>I'll be counting on you.</b>

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:20.350
<b>Very well.</b>

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:21.900
<b>Leave it to us!</b>

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:23.610
<b>What's your problem?</b>

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.500
<b>No, what's <i>yours</i>?!</b>

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:26.900
<b>Young Lord...</b>

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:28.150
<b>What is it?</b>

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.620
<b>Could you take me with you to the temple?</b>

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.290
<b>Huh? But the fighting has just ended.</b>

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.830
<b>You must be tired, right?</b>

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:39.830
<b>I'm fine.</b>

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:41.830
<b>Young Lord,</b>

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:48.380
<b>once this war is over, 
you'll be going to Zhcted, right?</b>

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:49.050
<b>Yeah.</b>

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.220
<b>I'm already so old.</b>

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:54.970
<b>Although I would love to follow you anywhere you go in Brune—</b>

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:58.930
<b>no, even beyond that and to the ends of the earth—</b>

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.560
<b>my body cannot keep up.</b>

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:08.070
<b>So please let me stay by your side
as much as possible during this war.</b>

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.160
<b>Okay then.</b>

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.200
<b>But promise me that if things get
dangerous, you'll turn heel at once.</b>

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:18.870
<b>I can still run away with the best of them!</b>

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.370
<b>Well, I'll go get ready.</b>

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.170
<b>My word.</b>

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.050
<b>Now we have a princess
<i>and</i> an old man as baggage.</b>

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.840
<b>Guess I really should come as well.</b>

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:31.840
<b>What?</b>

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:35.810
<b>My future depends on how this all turns out too.</b>

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:38.140
<b>Is there any reason why I shouldn't go with you?</b>

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.100
<b>Elen, please think about who you are!</b>

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:43.900
<b>We of higher standing need to maintain dignity.</b>

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:46.070
<b>You seem to be forgetting that you're a war maiden.</b>

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:51.400
<b>Lim, can you put together an 
escort of five that'd be stronger than me?</b>

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:57.540
<b>This is an extremely important mission, remember?</b>

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:01.410
<b>Depending on the outcome, our cause may be seen as just beyond reproach.</b>

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.920
<b>I won't sit here and wait.</b>

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.040
<b>I'm going with them.</b>

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:13.050
<b>Just in case:</b>

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:20.310
<b>If we run into trouble, save yourself first.
Only then should you try to rescue Princess Regin.</b>

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:21.680
<b>Got it?</b>

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:24.310
<b>Yeah, I got it.</b>

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.120
<b>That's a really small temple.</b>

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.440
<b>Please push it slowly.</b>

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:33.760
<b>It's chilly down here.</b>

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:35.590
<b>This almost looks like an escape tunnel.</b>

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.800
<b>It probably is one.</b>

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:40.810
<b>Before the Kingdom of Brune was established,</b>

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:44.520
<b>Artesium served as a stronghold
for the powerful families ruling the area.</b>

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.680
<b>Or so it's said.</b>

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:52.530
<b>What is it?</b>

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.950
<b>What are these pictures?</b>

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.160
<b>They depict the gods in battle with a dragon.</b>

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:14.380
<b>In ancient times, dragons were considered the only beings that could harm a god.</b>

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:21.930
<b>As someone from Zhcted, whose founder
supposedly was the incarnation of a dragon,</b>

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:25.020
<b>I have some pretty mixed feelings about that.</b>

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.230
<b>The gods did not always fight the dragons.</b>

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.230
<b>They sometimes tried to negotiate with them.</b>

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:35.400
<b>In our legends, the three Pillar Goddesses
were created to serve the dragons.</b>

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:41.370
<b>If this mural is here, the Holy Grotto should be...</b>

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:42.530
<b>...nearby, right?</b>

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:43.910
<b>Yes.</b>

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.210
<b>You're here.</b>

