00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:19.490
<b>I see.</b>

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:22.780
<b>So you really are alive, Prince Regnas.</b>

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.780
<b>Or should I say, Princess Regin?</b>

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:27.700
<b>What are you doing here?</b>

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.540
<b>How much do you know?</b>

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:33.290
<b>There's little point in having a conversation...</b>

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:36.050
<b>with the dead.</b>

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:37.670
<b>Your Highness!</b>

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:38.800
<b>Regin, stay back!</b>

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:42.680
<b>Quickly!</b>

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.240
<b>Steed, go!</b>

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.460
<b>Ryurik, can you hold them back?</b>

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.960
<b>If that's your order!</b>

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:14.960
<b>All right!</b>

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:03.260
<b>You're wonderfully skilled.</b>

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:06.090
<b>Despite an ally blocking your sight,</b>

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:08.260
<b>being in a poorly lit environment</b>

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:11.270
<b>with a ceiling this low,
and our soldiers advancing on you,</b>

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:17.400
<b>you were able to precisely target
my head and loose a powerful shot.</b>

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:21.690
<b>It seems you actually earned your title of Silvrash.</b>

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:24.700
<b>Stand aside, common soldiers.</b>

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:30.080
<b>Count Vorn and Princess Regin are the only ones I came to kill.</b>

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:34.580
<b>What kind of knights would we be if we stood aside?</b>

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:41.710
<b>You have trained yourself well for someone
who probably is not even twenty years old.</b>

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:46.090
<b>And <i>you've</i> got some nerve,
poking around in caves at your age—</b>

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:47.800
<b>I <i>chose</i> to fight in this hole!</b>

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:51.810
<b>Because here I can make sure no enemy escapes!</b>

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:22.710
<b>What is that sound?</b>

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:37.430
<b>Fall back!</b>

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:45.940
<b>Ryurik, take care of Her Highness!</b>

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.620
<b>Young Lord, hurry!</b>

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.080
<b>Count Vorn!</b>

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:04.750
<b>You are...</b>

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:06.760
<b>going to...</b>

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.640
<b>die here.</b>

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:15.190
<b>Tigre!</b>

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:29.990
<b>Tigre!</b>

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.280
<b>Bertrand?</b>

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.000
<b>Bertrand!</b>

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:27.880
<b>Bertrand!</b>

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:34.470
<b>Young Lord.</b>

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:36.470
<b>Bertrand...</b>

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.700
<b>Are you unhurt, Young Lord?</b>

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.880
<b>Yeah, I'm fine.</b>

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:02.700
<b>Because you protected me, I'm not hurt at all.</b>

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:06.830
<b>Young Lord, your hand is so warm.</b>

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:10.550
<b>You really do appear to be safe,</b>

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:16.840
<b>which means the life of this
old man was not sacrificed in vain.</b>

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:21.680
<b>No, Bertrand! You're going home to Alsace!</b>

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.480
<b>You said so yourself, didn't you?!</b>

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:28.520
<b>Alsace... Ah, yes...</b>

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:33.110
<b>Spring will... will come soon,
and the green will return...</b>

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:36.860
<b>That's right. Spring is coming soon, so...</b>

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.370
<b>Lord Urs...</b>

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:48.130
<b>Your boy... your boy has grown into a fine, hardworking man.</b>

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:52.590
<b>He did well in defending Alsace, which you left to him,</b>

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:54.880
<b>and keeping the peace.</b>

00:17:55.150 --> 00:18:01.000
<b>I'm so pleased and proud of him.</b>

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.450
<b>Boy!</b>

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:10.610
<b>Boy!</b>

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:18.950
<b>When Lord Urs fell, there wasn't a single thing I could do.</b>

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:25.620
<b>And while I couldn't have
done anything, I was full of fear.</b>

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:31.300
<b>Would a fourteen-year-old boy
actually be able to govern Alsace?</b>

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:37.670
<b>Lord Mashas had his own territory and duties to take care of.</b>

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:43.010
<b>However, my fear was absolutely unfounded.</b>

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:49.100
<b>Boy, I mean, Young Lord,</b>

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:54.510
<b>you many times surpassed my greatest expectations.</b>

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:56.360
<b>So much that I'm embarrassed</b>

00:18:56.360 --> 00:19:02.570
<b>to so eagerly have taken over the role of your father in Lord Urs' place.</b>

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:14.290
<b>It seems Lord Urs' concerns were unfounded as well.</b>

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:18.340
<b>He feared you would focus
your attention only on Alsace.</b>

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:24.640
<b>But Young Lord, while you love Alsace,
you also look to the outside world.</b>

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:27.220
<b>I look... to the outside world...</b>

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:32.600
<b>And so... there's nothing left to worry about.</b>

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:35.230
<b>I was blessed with a fine lord.</b>

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:36.320
<b>Bertrand!</b>

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:41.130
<b>Young Lord, see to Titta.{get shipped}</b>

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:52.520
<b>What do we do once we enter Artesium?</b>

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:54.250
<b>Position ourselves above the Holy Grotto.</b>

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:57.880
<b>Tigre...</b>

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:07.390
<b>What is that?</b>

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:09.720
<b>Hurry!</b>

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:37.960
<b>Tigre!</b>

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:43.220
<b>Are you okay, Tigre?{Looks perfectly healthy to me.}{He just felt like taking a quick nap}</b>

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:48.430
<b>Elen...</b>

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:53.600
<b>You really know how to worry me.</b>

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:10.740
<b>Bring me some rope!</b>

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:29.370
<b>All of this started when Bertrand risked his life</b>

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:33.600
<b>and crossed the border to come and find Tigre.{crossed the border? Not sure what that means. Referring way back to E01 or some metaphor for life/death or...?}{The border between Brune and Zhcted.}</b>

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:38.230
<b>His words were what galvanized Tigre into action.</b>

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:44.280
<b>Count Roland, I'll get straight to the point:</b>

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:48.570
<b>Will he be back on his feet by tonight?</b>

00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:56.470
<b>Honestly, I don't know.</b>

